# Answer key for B8 t4_adversarial.sql - procedural PL/pgSQL, adversarial.
#
# WRITTEN FROM SOURCE BEFORE THE ANALYSER WAS RUN OVER THIS FILE.
# Conventions: all earlier decisions, OBJECTIVES.md rules 1-9, D-39..D-42 (decided
# 2026-10-04, not implemented). Variables are `var:<name>`; bands per edge (rule 5).

@ 19 S1 a function never called
origin mart.fn_never_called 0
value staging.customers.country_code -> mart.kpi_rollup.country_code identity

@ 31 S2 a trigger function never bound
forbid value staging.orders.status -> mart.events_log.kind identity | NEW has no table until CREATE TRIGGER binds one (D-41); no table may be guessed

@ 44 S3 one trigger function, bound to two tables
origin mart.trg_stamp 2
value staging.returns.id, staging.shipments.id -> mart.events_log.id identity

@ 67 S4 a function with its own search_path
origin mart.fn_pathed 0
value staging.ledger.account -> core.ledger.account identity
forbid value staging.ledger.account -> staging.ledger.account identity | the function's SET search_path = core decides `ledger`, not the script's path (D-23)

@ 80 S5 the real statement after a RAISE
origin mart.fn_noisy 0
value staging.customers.segment -> mart.kpi_rollup.segment identity
filter staging.customers.status -> mart.kpi_rollup
forbid value staging.customers.email -> mart.kpi_rollup.segment identity | the INSERT before it is the text of a RAISE

@ 92 S6 EXECUTE of a parameter
expect dynamic_sql EXECUTE:92 | the whole statement is p_sql (D-42; Oracle EXECUTE IMMEDIATE:267)

@ 104 S7 a write whose failure is swallowed
origin mart.fn_swallow 0
value core.dim_store.region -> mart.top_customers.region identity
expect suppressed_error mart.fn_swallow:105 | WHEN OTHERS THEN NULL: the absence of a write below proves nothing (rule 7)

@ 118 S8 PERFORM
forbid value staging.orders.amount -> <result>.amount identity | PERFORM discards its query's rows

@ 145 S9 the read sees the second body
value staging.customers.full_name -> mart.top_customers.full_name identity
forbid value staging.customers.email -> mart.top_customers.full_name identity | that body was dropped before the read (D-31)

@ 155 S10 a variable named like a column
origin mart.fn_shadow 1
value staging.payments.amount -> var:mart.fn_shadow.amount aggregated

@ 157 S11 the variable in VALUES
origin mart.fn_shadow 1
value var:mart.fn_shadow.amount -> mart.top_customers.revenue identity

@ 169 S12 a $body$-quoted body holding $$
origin mart.fn_tagged 0
value staging.orders.currency -> mart.kpi_rollup.level identity
